  "cli_result_text": "Files submitted. Summary of the retrieved chain relevant to the task:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain:**\n- `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 `get_request_handler`, reads `content-type` header and negotiates JSON vs form/multipart body parsing before dependency solving.\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `solve_dependencies`, `request_body_to_args`, `get_body_field`: converts the raw parsed body (dict/FormData) into per-field values, handling `embed`, missing/`None` values (falls back to `deepcopy(field.default)`), and required-field errors.\n- `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 `ModelField.validate`, the Pydantic v1/v2 compatibility shim; in v2 it wraps a `TypeAdapter` per field for validation, which governs union-type and nested-model coercion behavior.\n- `fastapi/params.py` \u2014 `Body`/`Form`/`File`/`Param` field-info classes controlling `embed`, `media_type`, alias, and default handling.\n- `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, used for outbound serialization (relevant contrast point vs. request-side expectations).\n- `fastapi/exceptions.py`, `fastapi/dependencies/models.py` \u2014 error shaping (`RequestValidationError`) and the `Dependant` model that carries body params.\n\n**httpx request encoding chain:**\n- `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_request`/`encode_json`: JSON body uses plain stdlib `json.dumps`, not Pydantic-aware; doesn't call `.model_dump()` on models, doesn't omit `None`, no `exclude_unset`/`exclude_none` equivalent.\n- `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__`: sets `Content-Type` only via `encode_request`'s returned headers; `None`/default values pass straight through if present in the dict.\n- `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 `build_request` plumbs `json=` from `post()`/`request()` down to `Request()`.\n\n**Key drift points** (for the report): (1) httpx's `json.dumps` chokes on raw Pydantic model instances \u2014 callers must `.model_dump(mode=\"json\")` themselves; (2) FastAPI's Pydantic v2 `ModelField.validate` via `TypeAdapter` is strict about `None` vs missing keys for `Optional` fields with defaults, while httpx sends whatever dict shape it's given (including explicit `None` for unset optionals if the caller included them); (3) union-type discrimination in Pydantic v2 (`discriminator`) requires exact key shapes that a manually-built httpx `json=` dict may not produce, causing 422s.",
